---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FeaturedBuild from '../components/FeaturedBuild.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import ProductCard from '../components/ProductCard.astro';
import {projects,projectsNewestFirst,products} from '../lib/catalog';
const featured=projectsNewestFirst[0];
const picks=projectsNewestFirst.slice(0,3);
const components=products.filter(p=>p.featured).slice(0,4);
---
<BaseLayout title="MAKHEX — Little parts. Big ideas." description="Explore electronics and robotics maker projects, genuine credited build media, mapped parts and an open community sharing workbench discoveries.">
<section class="hero">
 <div class="container hero-inner">
  <div class="hero-copy">
   <p class="hero-kicker"><span class="kicker-spark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span> THE FRIENDLY MAKER WORKSHOP</p>
   <h1>Ideas are good.<br/><em>Making</em> is better<span class="hero-period">.</span></h1>
   <p class="hero-lede">Little boards. Big ideas. Pick something fun to build, get a clear parts list, and learn from what other makers have tried.</p>
   <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/projects/">Explore the builds <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/shop/">Browse the parts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
   <div class="hero-footnote"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Build blueprints &amp; BOMs <span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Honest workbench notes</div>
  </div>
  <FeaturedBuild project={featured} total={projects.length}/>
 </div>
 <div class="container workshop-tray" aria-label="MAKHEX at a glance">
  <span class="tray-prompt"><span class="tray-icon" aria-hidden="true">✳</span> MADE FOR MAKERS, TINKERERS &amp; CURIOUS MINDS</span>
  <span><strong>{projects.length}</strong> project blueprints</span><span><strong>{products.length}</strong> parts to explore</span><span><strong>{projects.length}</strong> project forums</span>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="section section-projects">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading">
   <div><span class="eyebrow">01 / PICK YOUR NEXT ADVENTURE</span><h2>Something fun<br/>to <em>make today.</em></h2></div>
   <div class="section-side"><p>From browser tab to workbench. Find a blueprint, see its bill of materials, and find out what still needs testing.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See all {projects.length} builds <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="project-grid">{picks.map(p=><ProjectCard project={p}/>)}</div>
  <p class="section-qualification"><span aria-hidden="true">ⓘ</span> Blueprints are starting ideas, not yet fully bench-verified kits.</p>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="section section-components"><div class="container">
 <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE PARTS DRAWER</span><h2>Good stuff,<br/><em>small packages.</em></h2></div><div class="section-side"><p>Boards, sensors, displays, and the little things that make big ideas work. Specs and sourcing are clearly labeled until verified.</p><a class="text-link" href="/shop/">Open the parts drawer <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
 <div class="product-grid">{components.map(p=><ProductCard product={p}/>)}</div>
 <div class="catalog-note"><span class="qualification-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> LOOKING ONLY: THESE ARE RESEARCH CANDIDATES, NOT ORDERABLE PRODUCTS.</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-method"><div class="container method-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / THE MAKHEX WAY</span><h2>More making.<br/><em>Less guessing.</em></h2><p>We love a clever component as much as anyone. But a parts list means more when it comes with a plan and real feedback from the bench.</p><a href="/about/" class="text-link">Get to know MAKHEX <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
 <ol class="method-list"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Find your “what if?”</h3><p>Pick a real-world gadget you’d love to have on your desk.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Know what goes inside.</h3><p>Check the BOM, expected wiring, and parts that still need validation.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Build it, then share.</h3><p>Learn what works, document what doesn’t, and help someone else.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="section home-blog-section"><div class="container">
 <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / FROM THE WORKBENCH</span><h2>Ideas worth<br/><em>building on.</em></h2></div><div class="section-side"><p>Practical reading for curious hands. Start with a plan, then test it on real hardware.</p><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">Read the MAKHEX blog <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
 <a class="home-blog-feature" href="/blog/robotics-engineer-six-month-roadmap/"><span class="home-blog-feature-stamp">MAKHEX BLOG <span>01 / LEARNING PATHS</span></span><span class="home-blog-feature-body"><strong>Learn robotics in 6 months.<br/>One real build at a time.</strong><span>Electronics → ESP32 → CAD → ROS 2 → robot learning. A practical roadmap, verified resources, and honest milestones.</span></span><span class="home-blog-feature-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</div></section>
<section class="section community-callout"><div class="container community-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">MADE BETTER TOGETHER</span><h2>Got a build?<br/><em>Show us.</em></h2><p>The crooked first version, the brilliant fix, the unexpected LED blink. This is the good stuff.</p><a href="/community/" class="btn btn-light">Visit the maker community <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="community-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="community-hand">✳</span><span class="community-doodle">Let's make<br/>something!</span><span class="community-spark">✺</span></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
